rota lap 4363, row 3 -- Water, the row that tastes; threshold, Brix infuse, the happy zone and the thin edge, growing a language. What it surfaced: taste only works up close, so this lap ran every instrument it cites rather than quoting a number, and the happy-zone page named the split the assert census turned up.
think Opened cold detached with the runner's own --detach, so the transcript name came from the tool rather than from my hand. 199 guards, 1818s, 194 green, 2 red, 3 gated, tree_moved=no.
think Reds first. stash_record red: stash@{0} held a lap of mine from 15:31 -- log, account shelf, index row, and one template-manifest.bron line -- run GREEN and never landed. Restored by tree rather than blob, since git show <ref>:<path> drops mode and the exec-bit law names that trap.
think The manifest line declined to ride, and reading why found the second red. Two peers had each landed allow context/BHAKTA_STYLE.md while my lap sat parked -- c96332c19 at 16:55:10 and c860fee71 at 17:28:44 -- so HEAD carried one path on two rows against the manifest's own header sentence, every tracked root path carries exactly one verdict.
think Kept the earlier row, beside RADIANT_STYLE.md and TWILIGHT_STYLE.md where it belongs; dropped the later one, which had landed between APARIGRAHA and BREACH. A sort | uniq -d over every verdict line reads one duplicate in the whole 251-rule manifest, and it was that one.
think Then the lap my elder card block named: amphora's unnamed asserts. Measured per file with the sweep scan's own awk predicate rather than a fresh one, so the reading and the guard agree by construction.
obs THREE HANDS REPAIRED ONE LINK IN ONE EVENING. Two landed and one parked, and the artifact kept the scar. This is the claim question the card has asked seventeen times, in its sharpest form yet: nothing in the ledger said the repair was being worked, so three ships each found the same red within three hours.
obs THE SPLIT IS WORTH MORE THAN THE COUNT. Of amphora's 45 unnamed asserts outside the CLI, 29 sat inside a run_selftest body and 16 in module code. A round-trip proof living inside its module reads to the sweep exactly like an unstated construction contract -- the happy zone and the thin edge, showing up in an assert census. rune_assert_sweep already counts *_witness.rye apart for that reason; a selftest inside a module has no such door.
obs 56 COMMENT LINES MOVED THE GRADE ZERO. qa_report_card read 94/91/91/91/94/91 across the six modules before, and the identical six numbers after, at the same service reading. The card grades a program on its comments and cannot see whether an assert names its reason -- a reading nobody takes, one room over from GRASS's declared-style line.
obs WHAT I DID NOT TAKE. src/main.rye holds all 85 remaining unnamed asserts and is the CLI's own lap; a duplicate_rows reading for the manifest is one firing so far, so it stays a lantern rather than a loom.
obs THE FIFTH FIRING OF A LOOM THAT ALREADY EXISTS. Both shelves I wrote carried climbing links at the depth of the pin they were folded out of -- archive/X.md inside a file already in construction/archive/ -- and the hot pass reddened fold_shelf_link_repoint. The repair was one command, sh tools/f/fold_shelf_link_repoint.sh --apply, three links, rescan fold_depth_lost 3 -> 0. The tool was built on 20260907 because four hands made this same fault in a week; I made it twice in one lap and paid one command for it.
obs AGAINST MYSELF, AND IT COST TWENTY MINUTES. Rather than wait out the red hot pass I reached for a signal on my own pid through fleet_call --signal TERM. It did not take on the first two sends, the pass crawled three guards in twelve minutes, and then died without writing a run_verdict -- a transcript with no verdict, which is exactly the wreck the baton names. Waiting was the right move from the first second; the bounded helper made the signal safe for peers and did nothing to make it wise.
